activities:
  # Day -2: Setting pieces in motion
  - type: note
    priority_ref: containment
    title: "Weekly threat digest - mostly harmless"
    created: "-2d"
    notes:
      - created: "-2d 09:30"
        content: |
          **From: GCHQ Automated Briefing <briefing@gchq.gov.uk>**
          **Subject: Weekly Threat Assessment - Week 3**

          The usual chatter. Russian botnet activity (same as last week). Iranian phishing campaigns (amateur hour). Chinese economic espionage (professionally tedious).

          One item worth a second glance: Uptick in comms around old Curtain network. Probably nothing. Dormant since '09.

          Filed under: things that will bite someone in the arse if ignored.
        source:
          type: email
          title: Weekly Threat Assessment - Week 3
          href: mailto:briefing@gchq.gov.uk
    tags:
      pinned: [user]

  - type: action
    author_ref: user
    priority_ref: team
    title: "River - check old East German networks"
    assignee_ref: river
    on: "-2d"
    notes:
      - author_ref: user
        created: "-2d 10:00"
        content: |
          Asked River to pull old files on defunct GDR networks. Didn't tell him why. Let him think it's busywork.

          He'll figure it out or he won't. Either way, I need someone looking at this who doesn't know they're looking at it.

  - type: event
    priority_ref: containment
    title: "Call: Whelan (Regent's Park)"
    at: "-2d 11:15 / -2d 11:23"
    notes:
      - created: "-2d 11:30"
        content: |
          Whelan fishing for information about Slough House workload. Asked if we had "capacity for additional oversight duties."

          Translation: Regent's Park wants to bury something with us.

          Told him we're drowning in paperwork. Which is true. Didn't mention we could handle it anyway. Let him think he's doing us a favour when he sends it over.
        source:
          type: call
          title: Call with James Whelan
    tags:
      question: [user]

  - type: note
    priority_ref: personal
    title: "GP surgery - missed call"
    created: "-2d"
    notes:
      - created: "-2d 14:30"
        content: |
          **Voicemail from NHS Appointments**

          "Mr Lamb, this is regarding your blood pressure follow-up. We haven't heard from you. Please call to schedule..."

          [Deleted]
        source:
          type: voicemail
          title: NHS Appointments

  # Day -1: Pieces moving
  - type: note
    author_ref: river
    priority_ref: team
    title: "GDR network files - pulled as requested"
    created: "-1d 09:00"
    notes:
      - author_ref: river
        created: "-1d 09:00"
        content: |
          Pulled the old GDR Curtain network files for Jackson. Not sure what he's looking for, but here's what I found:

          - Network supposedly dismantled 2009
          - East German sleepers, rolled up during reunification
          - Files closed, everyone accounted for

          One odd detail: Hans Wetzel (Asset CUR-17) listed as "presumed deceased" after a fire in Leipzig, May 2009. No body recovered. Case closed on presumption.

          Academic exercise or is there something here?

  - type: action
    author_ref: user
    priority_ref: containment
    title: "Review Curtain network files - something's off"
    assignee_ref: user
    on: "-1d"
    tags:
      urgent: [user]
    notes:
      - author_ref: user
        created: "-1d 10:15"
        content: |
          River pulled the files. Thorough work.

          Curtain network: Supposedly dismantled 2009. East German sleepers, rolled up during reunification cleanup. Everyone accounted for, files closed.

          Except the chatter says otherwise. Someone's activated an old protocol. Either:
          1. We missed someone (embarrassing)
          2. Someone found the protocol and is playing dress-up (dangerous)
          3. This is a provocation to see who responds (clever)

          Need to know which without letting anyone know I'm looking.

  - type: event
    priority_ref: team
    title: "Louisa - coffee, downstairs"
    at: "-1d 14:30 / -1d 14:42"
    notes:
      - created: "-1d 14:50"
        content: |
          Louisa's good at reading between lines. Mentioned the Curtain network in passing, like it was trivia. Watched her make the connections.

          She knows someone who might know someone. Didn't ask who. Don't need to.

          She'll make inquiries. Quietly. That's why she's useful.
        mentions:
          - louisa
    tags:
      pinned: [user]

  - type: action
    author_ref: user
    priority_ref: team
    title: "Roddy - trace old signal patterns"
    assignee_ref: roddy
    on: "-1d"
    notes:
      - author_ref: user
        created: "-1d 15:15"
        content: |
          Asked Roddy to look for old East German signal patterns in current intercepts. Told him it's for "historical analysis."

          He'll spend three days building an algorithm and emerge thinking he's a genius. Which is fine. I need the data, not the credit.

  - type: note
    priority_ref: admin
    title: "Budget report - due next week"
    created: "-1d"
    notes:
      - created: "-1d 11:00"
        content: |
          **From: Finance Department <finance@sloughhouse.gov.uk>**
          **Subject: FY2025 Q1 Budget Report - Due 31 Jan**

          Please submit your quarterly budget report including itemized expenses and headcount justification.

          Thrilling.
        source:
          type: email
          title: Budget Report Request
          href: mailto:finance@sloughhouse.gov.uk

  - type: event
    priority_ref: containment
    title: "Taverner - 'courtesy call'"
    at: "-1d 16:45 / -1d 16:52"
    notes:
      - created: "-1d 17:00"
        content: |
          Diana called to "touch base." Which means she wants something or she's worried I want something.

          Mentioned she's concerned about "historical network security." Interesting timing.

          So Regent's Park knows something's happening with Curtain. Question is: are they ahead of it or behind it?

          Told her Slough House remains committed to filing paperwork correctly. She laughed. Neither of us meant it.
        mentions:
          - taverner
    tags:
      warning: [user]

  # Day 0 (Base date): The work gets real
  - type: note
    priority_ref: containment
    title: "OPERATION CURTAIN CALL - active situation"
    on: "+0d"
    tags:
      urgent: [user]
      pinned: [user]
      decision: [user]
    notes:
      - created: "+0d 09:00"
        content: |
          ## Situation Summary

          **What we know:**
          - Old GDR sleeper network (Curtain) supposedly dead since 2009
          - Recent activation of old protocols detected in GCHQ intercepts
          - Regent's Park is aware and nervous
          - Three potential scenarios (see -1d notes)

          **What we've learned (last 48hrs):**
          - Louisa's contact confirms: two former Curtain assets made contact with handlers last week
          - Roddy found signal pattern matches - someone using exact GDR encryption schema
          - River's file review: one asset never properly accounted for - Hans Wetzel, dropped off radar 2009

          **Working theory:**
          Wetzel stayed dark for 15 years. Something triggered reactivation. Either he's being reactivated by external actor OR he's activating himself (why now?).

          **Problem:**
          Regent's Park will want to bring in heavy machinery. Surveillance teams, arrests, headlines. That'll spook whoever's actually running this.

          **Better approach:**
          Let them think we're watching the wrong thing. Meanwhile:
          - River tracks Wetzel's old associates (he'll think it's academic research)
          - Louisa works her contact network (she'll think she's helping)
          - Roddy monitors signals (he'll think he's showing off)
          - Shirley ready for physical surveillance if needed (she'll think she's finally getting real work)

          **My job:**
          Keep Regent's Park looking the wrong direction. Keep my team from knowing they're the right direction.

          If this works, nothing happens. No arrests. No headlines. Wetzel goes back to sleep or gets quietly retired.

          That's the job.
        mentions:
          - louisa
          - river
          - roddy
          - shirley
      - created: "+0d 09:20"
        content: |
          ---

          **@plot, what did we decide about Hans Wetzel in the 2009 review?**
        ai_query: true
      - created: "+0d 09:20"
        content: |
          **Plot AI Response:**

          Based on the 2009 Curtain Network Dissolution Review:

          Hans Wetzel (Asset CUR-17) was flagged as "presumed deceased" after his last known address in Leipzig burned down in May 2009. No body recovered. German police ruled it accidental (faulty wiring).

          Review committee decision: "Close file pending remains identification."

          **Note:** No follow-up confirmation ever filed. Case closed on presumption, not evidence.

  - type: event
    priority_ref: team
    title: "Team meeting - vague instructions"
    at: "+0d 10:00 / +0d 10:17"
    notes:
      - author_ref: user
        created: "+0d 10:25"
        content: |
          Assignments delivered with appropriate vagueness:

          - **River**: Continue archival research on defunct networks. "Historical value."
          - **Louisa**: Maintain relationships with former contacts. "Good practice."
          - **Roddy**: Pattern analysis on legacy encryption. "Training exercise."
          - **Shirley**: Standby for potential field work. "Maybe."
          - **Catherine**: Keep the office running. "As always."

          River questioned whether this connects to anything real. Everything's connected to everything. Technically true.

          Louisa knows something's happening. That's fine. She won't say.
      - author_ref: river
        created: "+0d 10:30"
        content: |
          Got another vague archival assignment from Jackson. "Historical value." Right.

          Something's up. He wouldn't be pulling old GDR files for no reason.
      - author_ref: louisa
        created: "+0d 10:32"
        content: |
          Jackson's running something quiet. Pattern analysis, archival research, field prep. He's building toward something without telling us what.

          I'll do what he asked. And I'll keep my eyes open.

  - type: action
    priority_ref: containment
    title: "Feed Regent's Park false priority"
    assignee_ref: user
    on: "+0d"
    notes:
      - created: "+0d 11:00"
        content: |
          Called Whelan. Mentioned Slough House picked up "concerning chatter" about Russian botnet activity potentially targeting infrastructure.

          It's real chatter (from the weekly briefing), just not particularly concerning. But it's the kind of thing that makes bureaucrats feel important.

          Regent's Park will spin up a task force, write reports, have meetings. Keep them busy and feeling productive.

          Meanwhile, I handle Curtain quietly.
        mentions:
          - whelan

  - type: note
    author_ref: catherine
    priority_ref: admin
    title: "Expense report - taxi receipts"
    created: "+0d"
    notes:
      - author_ref: catherine
        created: "+0d 12:15"
        content: |
          Jackson, you need to submit last month's expenses. I can't process the office budget until you do.

          I know you have taxi receipts somewhere. Please find them.
        source:
          type: email
          title: Expense Report Reminder
          href: mailto:catherine.standish@sloughhouse.gov.uk

  - type: event
    priority_ref: personal
    title: "Lunch - pub, alone"
    at: "+0d 13:00 / +0d 14:15"
    notes:
      - created: "+0d 14:30"
        content: |
          Steak and kidney pie (questionable kidney provenance). Three pints (questionable life choices).

          Thinking time. The work requires long periods of looking like you're doing nothing.

  # Day +1: Threads tightening
  - type: action
    priority_ref: containment
    title: "Analyze Roddy's signal intercepts"
    assignee_ref: user
    on: "+1d"
    tags:
      urgent: [user]
    notes:
      - created: "+1d 10:30"
        content: |
          Roddy's algorithm actually found something useful (don't tell him, it'll go to his head).

          Signal pattern matches from three locations:
          1. Leipzig (expected - Wetzel's old stomping ground)
          2. London (unexpected - someone local)
          3. Berlin (could be handler, could be coordination)

          London signal is the interesting one. Someone in the UK is part of this. Either:
          - Wetzel is here (ballsy)
          - Someone's coordinating with Wetzel (smart)
          - This is bigger than one washed-up GDR asset (problematic)

          Need to identify London source without tipping anyone off.
        mentions:
          - roddy

  - type: event
    priority_ref: team
    title: "Shirley - field assignment prep"
    at: "+1d 11:30 / +1d 11:45"
    notes:
      - created: "+1d 11:50"
        content: |
          Told Shirley she might need to do some "light observation" in the next few days. Didn't specify what or where.

          She's eager. Too eager. But she's good at not being seen, which is the skill we need.

          Told her: "Look bored. Be invisible. Report what you see, not what you think it means."

          She'll do fine.
        mentions:
          - shirley

  - type: note
    priority_ref: containment
    title: "Louisa update - former asset locations"
    created: "+1d"
    notes:
      - created: "+1d 13:15"
        content: |
          **Secure message from Louisa:**

          "Two former Curtain assets confirmed contact with old handler last week. Both refused reactivation. Both nervous.

          One mentioned a name: 'Der Geist' (The Ghost). Could be Wetzel, could be code name for someone else.

          Handler asked about 'the London arrangement.' They didn't know what that meant.

          - L"

          ---

          So there IS a London connection. And Wetzel (if it's him) is looking for something or someone here.

          This is getting interesting.
        source:
          type: secure_message
          title: Louisa - Curtain Update
        mentions:
          - louisa
    tags:
      warning: [user]

  - type: action
    priority_ref: team
    title: "River - research London GDR connections"
    assignee_ref: user
    on: "+1d"
    notes:
      - created: "+1d 14:00"
        content: |
          Gave River a new assignment: research any GDR operations that had London components during the Cold War.

          Framed it as: "Historical curiosity. Might be useful someday."

          He's smart enough to find the connections. Not yet smart enough to see the pattern. That'll come.
        mentions:
          - river

  - type: event
    priority_ref: admin
    title: "Budget meeting (unavoidable)"
    at: "+1d 15:00 / +1d 15:47"
    notes:
      - created: "+1d 16:00"
        content: |
          Finance wants to know why Slough House needs its budget maintained when we "don't do anything important."

          Explained that doing nothing important is expensive when done correctly.

          They weren't amused. Approved the budget anyway. They always do. Slough House is a convenient line item for hiding things.

  - type: note
    priority_ref: personal
    title: "Medical - another missed call"
    created: "+1d"
    notes:
      - created: "+1d 17:30"
        content: |
          **Voicemail from Dr. Mehta**

          "Mr Lamb, your blood pressure readings from last visit were concerning. We really need to discuss treatment options. Please call..."

          [Deleted]

          I'll die on my own schedule, thank you.
        source:
          type: voicemail
          title: Dr. Mehta - Follow-up

  # Day +2: Pieces in play
  - type: note
    priority_ref: containment
    title: "River's findings - London connection identified"
    created: "+2d"
    tags:
      urgent: [user]
      pinned: [user]
    notes:
      - created: "+2d 09:15"
        content: |
          **From: River Cartwright**

          Jackson,

          Found something in the London archives. Operation LINDEN - 1987-1989. GDR ran a small network in London focused on defence contractor intelligence.

          Network dissolved after the Wall fell, but one safehouse was never officially closed. Property in Shoreditch, purchased through shell company. Still owned by the same shell.

          Address: 47B Kingsland Road.

          Probably nothing, but thought you'd want to know.

          - River

          ---

          Definitely not nothing.
        source:
          type: email
          title: "Re: London GDR Research"
          href: mailto:river.cartwright@sloughhouse.gov.uk
        mentions:
          - river

  - type: action
    priority_ref: containment
    title: "Shirley - observe 47B Kingsland Road"
    assignee_ref: user
    on: "+2d"
    tags:
      urgent: [user]
      waiting: [user]
    notes:
      - created: "+2d 10:00"
        content: |
          Sent Shirley to watch the Shoreditch address. Instructions:

          - Don't approach
          - Don't engage
          - Look like you're waiting for someone who's late
          - Note anyone coming or going
          - Especially note anyone who looks like they're checking if they're being watched

          If Wetzel (or whoever) is using the old safehouse, they'll check surveillance. Shirley's job is to not look like surveillance.
        mentions:
          - shirley

  - type: event
    priority_ref: containment
    title: "Call: Taverner (escalation attempt)"
    at: "+2d 14:20 / +2d 14:33"
    notes:
      - created: "+2d 14:40"
        content: |
          Diana called, concerned about "historical network reactivation risks." Wants to "coordinate response."

          Translation: Regent's Park wants to take over.

          Told her Slough House is monitoring the situation (true) and there's no evidence of active threat (technically true - we don't have *evidence* yet, just strong suspicion).

          She doesn't believe me. I don't blame her. But she can't prove otherwise.

          Bought myself another 48 hours before she escalates to committee level.
        mentions:
          - taverner
    tags:
      blocked: [taverner]

  - type: action
    priority_ref: admin
    title: "Submit taxi receipts to Catherine"
    assignee_ref: user
    on: "+2d"
    notes:
      - created: "+2d 15:30"
        content: |
          Found receipts in jacket pocket (slightly stained, mostly legible).

          Catherine will make them work. She always does.
        mentions:
          - catherine

  - type: event
    priority_ref: team
    title: "Roddy - signal analysis update"
    at: "+2d 16:00 / +2d 16:12"
    notes:
      - author_ref: roddy
        created: "+2d 16:05"
        content: |
          Jackson, finished the signal pattern analysis. Built an algorithm to scan for old GDR encryption signatures.

          Results: Found matches in three locations - Leipzig, Berlin, and... Shoreditch, London. Someone's using original one-time pad materials from the 1980s.

          Fascinating historical data. Thought you'd find this interesting.
      - author_ref: user
        created: "+2d 16:20"
        content: |
          Roddy's analysis confirms it. London signals from Shoreditch area. Consistent with River's safehouse address.

          Someone's using the original GDR materials. Not a recreation. The actual one-time pads.

          Everything's coming together. Now we just need to know who's in the safehouse and what they want.

  - type: note
    priority_ref: containment
    title: "Working theory update - need to move soon"
    created: "+2d"
    tags:
      decision: [user]
    notes:
      - created: "+2d 17:00"
        content: |
          **@plot, summarize what we know about the Curtain situation**
        ai_query: true
      - created: "+2d 17:00"
        content: |
          **Plot AI Summary:**

          **Confirmed:**
          - Old GDR Curtain network showing signs of reactivation
          - Hans Wetzel (presumed dead 2009) likely alive and active
          - Active safehouse in London (47B Kingsland Road)
          - Signal intercepts confirm coordination between Leipzig, Berlin, and London
          - Code name "Der Geist" (The Ghost) in circulation
          - Former assets contacted but refused reactivation
          - Regent's Park aware but not yet taking action

          **Unknown:**
          - Wetzel's current objective
          - Who's running the reactivation (Wetzel solo? External handler?)
          - What "the London arrangement" refers to
          - Timeline for whatever they're planning

          **Recommended next steps:**
          - Await Shirley's surveillance report from Kingsland Road
          - Maintain Regent's Park misdirection
          - Prepare for quiet intervention if situation escalates
      - created: "+2d 17:05"
        content: |
          ---

          Good summary. Situation is nearly ready for resolution.

          Once Shirley reports back, I'll know whether this needs a quiet conversation or a quiet removal.

          Either way: no headlines, no credit, no mess. That's the standard.

  - type: note
    priority_ref: personal
    title: "Reminder: Catherine's birthday next month"
    created: "+2d"
    notes:
      - created: "+2d 18:00"
        content: |
          Need to remember this. She never mentions it, which means it matters.

          Something thoughtful. Not flowers (too obvious). Book, maybe.
        mentions:
          - catherine

  - type: action
    priority_ref: team
    title: "Weekly team review meeting"
    assignee_ref: user
    on: "+3d"
    recurrence_rule: "FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=FR"
    notes:
      - created: "+3d 10:00"
        content: |
          Friday ritual. Check in on the team without checking in too obviously.

          They think it's administrative. It is, in the sense that keeping them functional is administrative work.

  - type: note
    priority_ref: containment
    title: "Contingency: if Regent's Park moves first"
    created: "+2d"
    tags:
      warning: [user]
    notes:
      - created: "+2d 19:00"
        content: |
          If Diana escalates to committee before I wrap this:

          **Option A:** Share what we know, make it look like Slough House was building the case properly. Regent's Park gets the credit, Curtain gets messily resolved, headlines happen.

          **Option B:** Accelerate resolution. Move on safehouse immediately, contain before Regent's Park mobilizes. Riskier, but cleaner.

          **Option C:** Let Regent's Park have it, but fuck it up just enough that they need Slough House to clean up the mess. Satisfying, but petty.

          Prefer none of these. Prefer the quiet option. But contingencies exist for when preferences fail.
